Added a busy-time computation entry point: :func:`icalendar.busy_timeline` (and the :meth:`Calendar.busy_timeline <icalendar.Calendar.busy_timeline>` shortcut) synthesizes an actual free/busy timeline over a finite window from ``VAVAILABILITY``/``AVAILABLE`` rules, explicitly published ``VFREEBUSY`` periods and already scheduled events. Overlapping availability rules are combined according to :rfc:`7953#section-7` using ``PRIORITY`` (0 is the lowest precedence) and ``BUSYTYPE``, events honor ``TRANSP``/``STATUS``, and the result is a complete half-open UTC timeline of merged :class:`~icalendar.cal.busy_time.BusyPeriod` objects with per-segment provenance. Recurrence expansion is supplied through a callback instead of a new RRULE engine. I used AI to assist with this change.
